n\n" [:p {} "Luckily for Coughlin she was back on form in 2004 and, if not quite back to the level she showed two years earlier, was expected to win the Olympic title in the 100 metres backstroke. The American made her usual quick start and turned for home under her own world record pace. Coughlin began to made slightly down the home stretch and came under pressure from Zimbabwe’s " [:a {:href "/athletes/94046"} "Kirsty Coventry"] " out in lane one. Though Coventry closed down quickly on the tiring Coughlin she was unable to catch her but still had the consolation of winning her country’s first Olympic medal in an individual event. " [:a {:href "/athletes/103315"} "Laure Manaudou"] " the 400 metre freestyle champion, placed third with 2003 World Champion " [:a {:href "/athletes/47642"} "Antje Buschschulte"] " trailing in sixth."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "R1"] [:th {} "SF"] [:th {} "Final"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/103301"} "Natalie Coughlin"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/USA"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/USA.png"}] "USA"]] [:td {} "1:01.45 (1 h6)"] [:td {} "1:00.17 (1 h2)"] [:td {} "1:00.37 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/94046"} "Kirsty Coventry"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/ZIM"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/ZIM.png"}] "ZIM"]] [:td {} "1:01.60 (1 h3)"] [:td {} "1:01.21 (2 h1)"] [:td {} "1:00.50 (2)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Silver"} "Silver"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/103315"} "Laure Manaudou"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/FRA